See also references of EP     1085026A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU, NORIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU NORIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI NOBUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMOTSU, NORIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUNOUCHI, NOBUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A catalyst for polymerizing styrene and other monomer(s) which is capable of efficiently and inexpensively producing a styrene polymer having a syndiotactic structure.  The catalyst comprises (A) a transition metal compound, (B) an oxygenic compound and/or a compound capable of reacting with the transition metal compound to form an ionic complex, (C) a specific metal compound, preferably a specific organoaluminum compound represented by the following general formula: ((R&lt;1&gt;)3CO)n-Al-(R&lt;2&gt;)3-n (wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents a C1-30 aliphatic hydrocarbon group, a C6-30 aromatic hydrocarbon group, etc.; R&lt;2&gt; represents a hydrocarbon group; and n is 1 or 2), and (D) an alkylating agent which is used according to need.  The process for producing a styrene polymer comprises using the catalyst.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un catalyseur de polymérisation de styrène et autre(s) monomère(s) capable de produire de manière efficace et bon marché un polymère de styrène à structure syndiotactique. Le catalyseur comprend (A) un composé métallique de transition, (B) un composé oxygéné et/ou un composé pouvant réagir avec le composé métallique de transition pour former un complexe ionique, (C) un composé métallique spécifique, de préférence un composé d'organoaluminium spécifique représenté par la formule générale: ((R&lt;1&gt;)3CO)n-Al-(R&lt;2&gt;)3-n, (dans laquelle R1 représente un groupe hydrocarboné aliphatique C1-C30, un groupe hydrocarboné aromatique C6-C30, etc., R2 représente un groupe hydrocarboné; et n est égal à 1 ou 2) et (D) un agent d'alkylation utilisé selon les besoins. Ce procédé de production de polymère de styrène fait appel au catalyseur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>